From b4974c0f3fe06ec8a90d3032affa7c8d5fe6ed61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:22:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 178/206] feat: LPV geometry volume occlusion and sky light
 injection

- Geometry Volume (r_LPVOcclusion, default 1): RSM surfels accumulate a
  directional blocking potential per cell (accumulator widened 16 -> 20
  ints, additive cosine-lobe x face-coverage, self-normalizing), resolved
  into a dedicated 3D texture and applied as midpoint transmittance during
  propagation. First iteration runs unoccluded so light can leave the
  source cell. Suppresses light bleeding through walls/floors.
- Sky light (r_LPVSkyLight, default 0.25): cells passing a sun-visibility
  test against the RSM depth (open-sky proxy) receive a downward cosine
  lobe of sky colour. Interiors only get it through propagation via
  openings, attenuated by the GV - AO-like ambient. Energy is decoupled
  from r_LPVIntensity (value = target irradiance in sky-colour units on
  an upward-facing outdoor surface).
- r_LPVDebug 12: GV blocking potential surface mosaic.
- Docs: 05 v1.2 section, INDEX status refresh.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
